  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192632/assets/ce3b78035978226d9b095a4746d76b090a9225e2c6eaf20a6a19a2857c056f98.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the image of the graph $y=|x|$ under the action of a single translation. What is the equation of this curve?\n\nThe equation of this curve is\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that $y=|x-a|$ is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $a$ units right.\n\nNotice that here, the graph is moved *right* by $7$ units. This corresponds to $a=7.$\n\n Therefore, the equation of the curve is $y=|x-7|.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192632/assets/4be0b85e84626fa9960cb44017209b842cec090d1dfd409a290721a7250caf6c.png)",
